  },
  "description": "What: Step SLA under an alarm storm or steady alarm load: alarms due, applied/skipped per second, evaluator cycles and failed batches, its 3-connection DB pool, Postgres row updates, JVM and container. Step SLA runs have no k6: type the run id in \"Run id\" to show the runner's markers. How: provisioned by monitoring/docker-compose.yml or imported into CCE's Grafana (monitoring/cce-grafana-import/README.md). Needs: DS_PROMETHEUS with the cce-step-sla-service and postgres scrape jobs; runner annotations tagged cce-performance + run id. Outputs: nothing written; panels and run annotations only.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "id": null,
  "links": [
    {
      "asDropdown": true,
      "icon": "external link",
      "includeVars": true,
      "keepTime": true,
      "tags": ["cce-performance"],
      "targetBlank": false,
      "title": "CCE Performance dashboards",
      "tooltip": "",
      "type": "dashboards",
      "url": ""
    }
  ],
  "panels": [
    {
      "description": "Explains how to locate a seeded Step SLA run, which has no k6 metrics.",
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "Step SLA tests use **no k6**: the runner seeds alarms in Postgres and watches them ring. So there is no shaded k6 region and the *Run id* list is empty for these runs. **Type the run id** (e.g. `20261105-142233`, printed at the start of the run and in the results folder name) into *Run id* and press Enter, or open this dashboard with `&var-testid=<runId>` added to the URL. The green run markers (tags `cce-performance` + run id) then show seeding, first alarm ringing and catch-up.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Finding a Step SLA run",
      "type": "text",
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 3,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 3
      },
      "id": 2,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Alarms (not filtered by run)",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "SLA transition rows whose time has come and that the next cycle would fetch (gauge cce_sla_transitions_due). In a storm it jumps to the number of seeded alarms when they ring, then should fall to 0; the time that takes is the catch-up time. Observer effect: the service runs a SQL count for EVERY scrape (every 5 s here) on its 3-connection pool.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "axisBorderShow": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisColorMode": "text",
            "axisLabel": "",
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "gradientMode": "none",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "pointSize": 4,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "none"
            },
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "off"
            }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": ["mean", "max", "lastNotNull"],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "max(cce_sla_transitions_due)",
          "legendFormat": "due",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
